      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Michael Gunther",
      "description": "Alternate spelling: Kubyauk-gyi. The temple was built by Prince Rajakumar, the son of Kyanzittha, as an offering for the salvation of his father. The south face is seen in this photo. Its towers are of the Indian sikhara type; their tips are restored. The temple's date (1113) is recorded on an important inscription of Rajakumar, written in Pyu, Mon, Old Burman, and Pali. This is the earliest artifact (so far discovered) on which the Burmese language is written.",
      "dateCreated": "2014-09-03 13:39:21",
      "categories": [
        "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "Gubyaukgyi (Myinkaba)",
        "Self-published work"
      ],
